#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/vro.rst:70
msgid "Using vRealize Orchestrator"
msgstr "Usar vRealize Orchestrator"

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/vro.rst:72
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"One of the first things |morpheus| does when it is tied into a vRO "
"integration is sync all available workflows by category. These workflows "
"become available when creating a new |morpheus| task in "
":menuselection:`Library --> Automation`. |morpheus| allows a user to map "
"these vRO workflows into the task engine. The task engine allows users to"
" design workflows that chain tasks in order or operate at different "
"phases of a provisioning request. For more information on tasks, please "
"read the Automation documentation."
msgstr ""
"One of el primero things |morpheus| does cuando it es tied en un vRO "
"integration es sync todos disponible workflows by category. These "
"workflows become disponible cuando creating un nuevo |morpheus| task in "
"|LibAut|. |morpheus| allows un usuario to map estos vRO workflows en la "
"tarea engine. La tarea engine permite un los usuarios design workflows "
"que chain tasks in order o operate at diferente phases of un provisioning"
" solicitud. For más información on tasks, please read el Automation "
"documentación."

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/vro.rst:74
msgid "Creating a task for vRO is simple."
msgstr "Crear task for vRO is simple."

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/vro.rst:76
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First, go to :menuselection:`Library --> Automation` and create a new "
"task.  Enter a Name and a Code, the Code can be used later to reference "
"the results of tasks.  Choose a task type of ``vRealize Orchestrator "
"Workflow``. A dropdown will appear allowing one to first select the "
"active vRO Integration you would like to use. Once that is selected, a "
"list of workflows becomes available."
msgstr ""
"First, go to |LibAut| y create un nuevo task.  Enter un Name y un Code, "
"el Code puede be used later to referencia el resultados of tasks.  Choose"
" una tarea tipo of ``vRealize Orchestrator Workflow``. A desplegable será"
" appear allowing one to primero select el activo vRO Integration you "
"sería like to use. Once que es seleccionado, un lista of workflows "
"becomes disponible."

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/vro.rst:78
msgid ""
"The next part is where things can get a bit tricky. The parameter body "
"(expected in JSON) format can be a bit difficult to track down. One way "
"is to use the Network Chrome inspector when kicking off a sample workflow"
" from the vRO HTML5 client and grabbing the parameter JSON. Another is to"
" query the API yourself and look at the samples from historical run "
"history."
msgstr ""
"The siguiente part es donde things puede get un bit tricky. The parámetro"
" body (expected in JSON) formato puede be un bit difficult to track down."
" One way es to use el Network Chrome inspector cuando kicking off un "
"sample workflow desde el vRO HTML5 client y grabbing el parámetro JSON. "
"Another es to query el API yourself y look at el samples desde historical"
" run history."

